 "transcriber_notes": "SnowPilot chart, older layout ('Snow Pit Profile', 994x840 JPG). Height axis in the middle, 4.0 px/cm (ticks every 10 cm, 0 at y 751); boundaries from the bar outlines 125, 85, 84, 64, 52, 44, 32, 28, 18, 17, 5 (+-0.3 cm; thin layers are drawn taller in the table, with leaders). Hardness bars grow leftward from the height axis on a uniform axis (F 399, 4F 327, 1F 255, P 183, K 111, I 39 px; a third is 24 px): 84-52 cm end one third past 1F (1F+). Temperatures from the red dots on the top axis (-10 to 0 degC, 43.3 px per degree, 0 at the height axis), every 10 cm from 140 cm down (+-0.1 degC). No moisture column; the ρ column is blank. The test lines labelled 'Depth: (cm)' are drawn at those values on the height axis and the Stability Test Notes match the layers there (125 Jan 7 interface, 90 on DF, 18 IFrc), so they are heights. The Notes' 'Jan 1 SH down 65cm' is the 85-84 cm surface hoar layer (HS 150 - 65 = 85). Elevation printed 2030 m and aspect 359 on a 0 degree slope, copied as printed."
